Hallelujah!

3
00:00:13.238 --> 00:00:14.238
Amazing!

4
00:00:14.238 --> 00:00:15.238
Amazing!

5
00:00:15.238 --> 00:00:16.738
I found it an amazing month.

6
00:00:16.738 --> 00:00:17.738
Me too.

7
00:00:18.738 --> 00:00:19.738
There are then two.

8
00:00:20.738 --> 00:00:24.738
I really found it a wonderful month, but I say this for a reason...

9
00:00:25.238 --> 00:00:26.238
I say this for a reason...

10
00:00:27.738 --> 00:00:29.738
The month that we have...

11
00:00:32.238 --> 00:00:33.738
The month that we have...

12
00:00:34.738 --> 00:00:38.238
Makes lives completely different.

13
00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:41.738
The Word of God has so much potential.

14
00:00:42.738 --> 00:00:46.238
It has a wow potential. It has a boom potential.

15
00:00:47.238 --> 00:00:52.238
I have seen lives completely changed, including my own life,

16
00:00:52.238 --> 00:00:53.738
through the Word of God.

17
00:00:54.238 --> 00:00:58.738
And the only thing we need to do is repent to the Word of God.

18
00:00:58.738 --> 00:01:02.238
Repenting means that you change direction with a joyful heart.

19
00:01:02.738 --> 00:01:07.238
And that you say, it was like this before, and now in the name of Jesus we will approach it like this.

20
00:01:07.238 --> 00:01:12.238
And truly, that change of direction is amazing to see.

21
00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:16.238
I found it amazing to see how it had its effect in my own life,

22
00:01:16.238 --> 00:01:19.238
and every time I see people come to repentance,

23
00:01:19.238 --> 00:01:21.238
and take God seriously.

24
00:01:21.238 --> 00:01:22.738
It is really amazing.

25
00:01:24.738 --> 00:01:30.238
We have agreed together that we will talk openly about relationships once a year.

26
00:01:30.238 --> 00:01:35.238
And I think we will hold it in the month of November for the time being, in the coming years.

27
00:01:35.738 --> 00:01:41.238
And it is so important that we, in this society, in this world,

28
00:01:41.238 --> 00:01:44.738
now, precisely this, keep proclaiming.

29
00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:49.738
Whatever reactions come from it, we will keep saying it.

30
00:01:49.738 --> 00:01:51.738
For God's Word is the truth.

31
00:01:52.738 --> 00:01:54.238
God's Word is the truth.

32
00:01:54.738 --> 00:01:58.238
Comma, and the truth will set you free.

33
00:01:58.238 --> 00:01:59.738
In Jesus' name.

34
00:02:00.738 --> 00:02:06.238
So this month we have discussed various topics within relationships.

35
00:02:07.238 --> 00:02:09.238
Week 1 was about families.

36
00:02:09.738 --> 00:02:12.238
Week 2 was about dating.

37
00:02:12.738 --> 00:02:14.738
Week 3 was about parenting.

38
00:02:15.238 --> 00:02:18.238
And this is week 4, and it is about singles.

39
00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:23.238
And singles, single people,

40
00:02:23.738 --> 00:02:28.238
you might think of them,

41
00:02:28.238 --> 00:02:29.238
but that's not me.

42
00:02:29.738 --> 00:02:31.238
I am already married.

43
00:02:31.738 --> 00:02:33.238
But here is a newsflash.

44
00:02:33.738 --> 00:02:38.238
We are all single.

45
00:02:39.738 --> 00:02:43.238
The people who were at the Singles Connect Group yesterday,

46
00:02:43.238 --> 00:02:45.238
are all saying amen now.

47
00:02:45.738 --> 00:02:48.238
And they are all saying, yes, I already knew all of that.

48
00:02:49.738 --> 00:02:51.238
But then you still need to hear it once more.

49
00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:55.238
Because repetition is good for a person.

50
00:02:56.238 --> 00:03:00.238
But we are all single.

51
00:03:02.738 --> 00:03:06.238
You are single.

52
00:03:07.238 --> 00:03:09.238
How so Tim? I am married.

53
00:03:10.238 --> 00:03:12.238
No, you are alone.

54
00:03:12.738 --> 00:03:15.238
Because God has actually made you alone.

55
00:03:15.738 --> 00:03:17.238
He made you.

56
00:03:17.738 --> 00:03:21.238
He went to the cross for you.

57
00:03:21.738 --> 00:03:24.238
He rose for you.

58
00:03:24.738 --> 00:03:28.238
And he wants a relationship with you.

59
00:03:28.738 --> 00:03:30.738
And that is what you need to focus on.

60
00:03:31.238 --> 00:03:37.238
He does not want a relationship with your marriage either, understand me well.

61
00:03:37.738 --> 00:03:39.238
But He wants a relationship with you.

62
00:03:40.238 --> 00:03:45.238
You can never stand before the Lord later and say,

63
00:03:45.738 --> 00:03:47.238
yes, but we are okay, right?

64
00:03:47.738 --> 00:03:50.238
Because Vanessa loved you, didn't she?

65
00:03:50.738 --> 00:03:53.238
No, you stand before the Lord yourself.

66
00:03:53.238 --> 00:03:56.238
You have to maintain your own relationship with God.

67
00:03:56.738 --> 00:03:59.238
You are single.

68
00:03:59.738 --> 00:04:01.238
Let that be clear.

69
00:04:02.738 --> 00:04:05.238
And I say this at the beginning of this sermon,

70
00:04:05.738 --> 00:04:09.238
because I actually want to highlight a number of things,

71
00:04:09.738 --> 00:04:12.238
which I have already set down now,

72
00:04:12.738 --> 00:04:14.238
that we can all listen to here.

73
00:04:15.238 --> 00:04:19.238
This is not just for those who are not married yet.

74
00:04:20.238 --> 00:04:24.238
This is not just for those who may still hope for a marriage.

75
00:04:24.738 --> 00:04:26.238
This is for all of us.

76
00:04:26.738 --> 00:04:30.238
And in this last week, I want to teach from the book,

77
00:04:30.738 --> 00:04:32.238
from the letter ONE CORINTHIANS.

78
00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:34.238
Maybe you have your Bible with you.

79
00:04:34.738 --> 00:04:37.238
Then you can already go to ONE CORINTHIANS chapter 7.

80
00:04:37.738 --> 00:04:41.238
And because of the time, I have made a selection of two fragments.

81
00:04:41.738 --> 00:04:43.238
from 1 CORINTHIANS chapter 7.

82
00:04:43.738 --> 00:04:46.238
And I will read, in case you are taking notes.

83
00:04:46.238 --> 00:04:49.238
I will read from 1 CORINTHIANS chapter 7,

84
00:04:49.738 --> 00:04:51.738
verses 6 through 11.

85
00:04:52.738 --> 00:04:55.238
And then I will immediately continue, so I will keep reading.

86
00:04:55.738 --> 00:05:00.238
Then I will immediately continue to verses 25 through 35.

87
00:05:01.238 --> 00:05:02.238
That is quite a lot, Tim.

88
00:05:03.238 --> 00:05:04.238
Now I know.

89
00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:08.238
If you are there, say amen.

90
00:05:08.738 --> 00:05:09.738
That is quick.

91
00:05:14.238 --> 00:05:15.238
Here it comes.

92
00:05:16.238 --> 00:05:17.238
I, Paul,

93
00:05:18.738 --> 00:05:23.238
give you this as good advice, not as a command.

94
00:05:23.738 --> 00:05:27.238
I would like everyone to be unmarried, as I am.

95
00:05:27.738 --> 00:05:31.238
But each person has their own gifts from God.

96
00:05:31.738 --> 00:05:36.738
One has the gift of marriage, the other the gift of remaining unmarried.

97
00:05:37.238 --> 00:05:39.738
But to the unmarried and the widows I say,

98
00:05:40.238 --> 00:05:42.238
it is good to remain unmarried as I am.

99
00:05:42.738 --> 00:05:45.238
But if you find that too difficult, it is better to marry.

100
00:05:45.238 --> 00:05:52.238
For it is better to marry than to burn with passion.

101
00:05:52.738 --> 00:05:53.738
Yes, that is the Bible.

102
00:05:54.238 --> 00:05:57.738
But to the people who are married, the Lord gives the command, not I,

103
00:05:58.238 --> 00:06:00.238
that a woman must not separate from her husband.

104
00:06:00.738 --> 00:06:03.738
If she does, she must remain unmarried.

105
00:06:04.238 --> 00:06:07.738
Or go back to her husband and reconcile with him.

106
00:06:08.238 --> 00:06:12.238
And a man, likewise, must not separate from his wife.

107
00:06:13.738 --> 00:06:14.738
Verse 25.

108
00:06:15.238 --> 00:06:20.238
I have no command from the Lord regarding the unmarried girls, but I do have my own opinion.

109
00:06:20.738 --> 00:06:22.738
And thanks to God's Spirit, it is trustworthy.

110
00:06:23.238 --> 00:06:28.238
I think that because of the persecution that is to come, it is good to remain unmarried.

111
00:06:29.238 --> 00:06:33.238
If you are already engaged to a girl or are already married, do not separate.

112
00:06:33.738 --> 00:06:36.238
But if you do not have a wife, do not seek one.

113
00:06:37.238 --> 00:06:42.238
But if a boy and a girl marry, they do nothing wrong with that.

114
00:06:43.238 --> 00:06:49.238
However, they must take into account that they will have more difficulties and sorrow in the persecution.

115
00:06:49.738 --> 00:06:51.238
And I would rather spare them that.

116
00:06:51.738 --> 00:06:55.238
I say this, brothers and sisters, because there is very little time left.

117
00:06:55.738 --> 00:06:59.238
If you are married, let that not be the most important thing for you.

118
00:06:59.738 --> 00:07:03.238
If you are sad, do not give too much into that.

119
00:07:03.738 --> 00:07:06.738
If you are happy, do not forget all the other things.

120
00:07:07.238 --> 00:07:11.238
If you have bought something, let that not be the most important thing for you.

121
00:07:11.238 --> 00:07:17.238
If you use the things of this world, do not let yourself be influenced by them.

122
00:07:17.738 --> 00:07:20.238
For the world as it is now will not last much longer.

123
00:07:20.738 --> 00:07:23.238
I wish you did not have worries.

124
00:07:23.738 --> 00:07:27.238
An unmarried man can give all his time and attention to the work of the Lord.

125
00:07:27.738 --> 00:07:30.238
He tries to please God as much as possible.

126
00:07:30.738 --> 00:07:36.238
And a married man, but a married man, also gives time and attention to earthly things.

127
00:07:36.738 --> 00:07:39.238
For he also tries to please his wife.

128
00:07:39.238 --> 00:07:41.238
Thus he is divided.

129
00:07:41.738 --> 00:07:47.238
Widows and unmarried girls can give all their time and attention to the work for the Lord.

130
00:07:47.738 --> 00:07:50.238
They try to live for Him with all their heart and soul.

131
00:07:50.738 --> 00:07:55.738
But married women also give time and attention to earthly things, because they want to please their husband.

132
00:07:56.238 --> 00:07:58.238
I say this to help you.

133
00:07:58.738 --> 00:08:00.238
Not to make it difficult for you.

134
00:08:00.738 --> 00:08:04.238
I say it to make it clear to you what is good to do.

135
00:08:04.738 --> 00:08:10.238
And what is needed to serve the Lord with all your attention.

136
00:08:13.238 --> 00:08:14.238
That's intense, isn't it?

137
00:08:15.238 --> 00:08:20.238
And so in that last week, you think you are getting a dessert, and then you get this.

138
00:08:23.238 --> 00:08:24.738
I want to point something out.

139
00:08:25.238 --> 00:08:28.738
The Bible is composed of different kinds of books.

140
00:08:29.238 --> 00:08:33.238
The Bible comes from the word Biblios.

141
00:08:33.238 --> 00:08:36.238
And Biblios is the same as library, a collection of books.

142
00:08:37.238 --> 00:08:41.238
And each book has its own purpose.

143
00:08:41.738 --> 00:08:44.238
You write a book to convey a message.

144
00:08:44.738 --> 00:08:47.238
To make a message clear to the world.

145
00:08:47.738 --> 00:08:50.238
When you write a book it can be a biography.

146
00:08:50.738 --> 00:08:52.238
Or you can describe songs in it.

147
00:08:52.738 --> 00:08:54.238
Or you can describe history in it.

148
00:08:54.738 --> 00:08:59.238
But every time you write a book, even when you write factual history,

149
00:08:59.738 --> 00:09:02.738
you still want to say something with the history you write.

150
00:09:03.238 --> 00:09:04.238
Do you understand what I mean?

151
00:09:04.738 --> 00:09:07.738
You want to communicate something. You want people to learn something.

152
00:09:08.738 --> 00:09:12.238
In the Bible, you also have letters.

153
00:09:12.738 --> 00:09:17.238
And letters are often found in the New Testament.

154
00:09:17.738 --> 00:09:24.738
These letters have a very specific, laser-sharp purpose.

155
00:09:25.238 --> 00:09:27.738
They have their own context.

156
00:09:28.238 --> 00:09:30.238
It is intended for them.

157
00:09:30.738 --> 00:09:31.738
In their time.

158
00:09:31.738 --> 00:09:33.238
For this reason.

159
00:09:33.738 --> 00:09:38.238
Paul is therefore the pastor of the church in Corinth.

160
00:09:38.738 --> 00:09:44.238
And he writes, because all sorts of things are happening in that church, he writes a letter to them.

161
00:09:44.738 --> 00:09:46.238
We would just call.

162
00:09:46.738 --> 00:09:49.238
But at that time it really went through letters.

163
00:09:49.738 --> 00:09:56.238
And then you have to make sure that you write something on that very expensive piece of paper,

164
00:09:56.738 --> 00:09:59.738
that is very targeted.

165
00:09:59.738 --> 00:10:03.238
You can't just say, everything is fine with you and blah blah blah.

166
00:10:03.738 --> 00:10:05.238
That doesn't work, because you don't have time.

167
00:10:05.738 --> 00:10:08.238
Because you have to write everything jam-packed in your letter.

168
00:10:08.738 --> 00:10:10.238
So you don't go whining.

169
00:10:10.738 --> 00:10:12.238
You get straight to your point in such a letter.

170
00:10:12.738 --> 00:10:14.238
Do you understand what I mean?

171
00:10:14.738 --> 00:10:20.238
And 1 Corinthians 7 is something that Paul finds very important.

172
00:10:20.738 --> 00:10:25.238
To teach to the church in Corinth in the first century after Christ.

173
00:10:25.738 --> 00:10:29.238
Because of the behavior that is happening in the church in Corinth.

174
00:10:29.738 --> 00:10:31.238
Corinth.

175
00:10:31.738 --> 00:10:36.238
Not like Eindhoven, but more like Vegas.

176
00:10:36.738 --> 00:10:38.238
Sin City.

177
00:10:38.738 --> 00:10:40.238
Everything happened there.

178
00:10:40.738 --> 00:10:42.238
Everything could happen there.

179
00:10:42.738 --> 00:10:44.238
Everything also happened there.

180
00:10:44.738 --> 00:10:47.238
From good to very, very bad in Corinth.

181
00:10:47.738 --> 00:10:50.238
And those people came to repentance.

182
00:10:50.738 --> 00:10:53.238
Those people came to Jesus.

183
00:10:53.738 --> 00:10:56.238
Not nice people came to Jesus.

184
00:10:56.738 --> 00:10:58.238
Riffraff came to Jesus.

185
00:10:58.238 --> 00:10:59.738
Awesome.

186
00:11:00.238 --> 00:11:02.738
Because that is what Jesus loves the most.

187
00:11:03.238 --> 00:11:05.738
Prostitutes and tax collectors inside his congregation.

188
00:11:06.238 --> 00:11:07.738
That is why Jesus came.

189
00:11:08.238 --> 00:11:10.738
But when you get those people in.

190
00:11:12.238 --> 00:11:13.738
The person sitting next to you.

191
00:11:14.238 --> 00:11:16.738
They need instructions.

192
00:11:17.238 --> 00:11:23.738
We need instructions from God's Word on how to live for God.

193
00:11:23.738 --> 00:11:25.238
What makes Him happy.

194
00:11:25.738 --> 00:11:28.238
And what will ultimately make you happy as well.

195
00:11:28.738 --> 00:11:31.238
Making Him happy is becoming happy yourself.

196
00:11:31.738 --> 00:11:34.238
Making Him happy is becoming happy yourself.

197
00:11:34.738 --> 00:11:36.238
Do you understand what I mean?

198
00:11:36.738 --> 00:11:38.238
And this is what Paul writes.

199
00:11:38.738 --> 00:11:43.238
And the reason I say that what we just read is very contextual is.

200
00:11:43.738 --> 00:11:46.238
Is because Paul himself also understands.

201
00:11:46.738 --> 00:11:51.238
That everything he says is about relationships.

202
00:11:51.238 --> 00:12:04.738
And relationships are all 100% individual, contextual to what you have experienced or will experience in your life.

203
00:12:05.238 --> 00:12:06.738
I will say it once more.

204
00:12:07.238 --> 00:12:14.738
Your life is 100% different from the life of the person sitting next to you right now.

205
00:12:15.738 --> 00:12:25.238
Your life is made up of things that happened to your parents and perhaps even your grandparents and the ancestors, that's what it's called.

206
00:12:25.738 --> 00:12:31.238
And the things you have experienced and learned and all those components come together.

207
00:12:31.738 --> 00:12:39.238
School, family, household, uncles and aunts, church, no church, politics, and everything comes together nowadays.

208
00:12:39.238 --> 00:12:44.738
Media, social media, it all gets thrown at you and that shapes who you are.

209
00:12:45.238 --> 00:12:52.738
All the things you experience and receive shape the person you are now as you sit here.

210
00:12:53.238 --> 00:12:58.738
And everything you have experienced also shapes the choices you have made yourself.

211
00:12:59.238 --> 00:13:08.738
Based on good education, based on a good upbringing, based on not such a good upbringing, based on disappointments.

212
00:13:09.238 --> 00:13:11.738
That ensures that you are who you are now.

213
00:13:12.238 --> 00:13:19.738
And that is why we are Open Church, because you are received openly to be who you are.

214
00:13:20.238 --> 00:13:23.738
But we do not leave you as you are.

215
00:13:24.238 --> 00:13:28.738
Here you are trained to be a child of God and to love Him.

216
00:13:29.238 --> 00:13:31.738
The training we do here is to learn to love Him.

217
00:13:32.238 --> 00:13:35.738
The change is His work in Jesus' name. Hallelujah.

218
00:13:36.238 --> 00:13:37.238
Good job.

219
00:13:38.238 --> 00:13:46.238
Contextual is very important, because you see Paul also regularly say, I say this as my own opinion.

220
00:13:46.738 --> 00:13:53.238
What we just read, verses 6 to 11 and 25 to 35, there Paul says a few times very clearly,

221
00:13:53.738 --> 00:13:57.238
Listen boys, this is my opinion, this is not a command.

222
00:13:57.738 --> 00:14:04.238
And then he says, come on, but because I am filled with God's Spirit, this is quite a good opinion.

223
00:14:05.738 --> 00:14:08.238
And I believe that this is not arrogance.

224
00:14:08.738 --> 00:14:18.238
I believe that if you are filled with God's Spirit and if you have the same solid knowledge of God's Word as Paul had,

225
00:14:18.738 --> 00:14:22.238
then you may very well express your opinion.

226
00:14:22.738 --> 00:14:30.238
For your opinion, if you pray with the Father, if you read God's Word and you are filled with the Spirit, then your opinion is fine.

227
00:14:31.238 --> 00:14:35.738
And I would like Christians to speak up in Jesus' name.

228
00:14:36.238 --> 00:14:43.738
Speak Christians in Jesus' name. Speak in your business in Jesus' name. Speak at your school in Jesus' name.

229
00:14:44.238 --> 00:14:51.738
Speak, let your opinion be heard in Jesus' name. I declare this as a prophecy over your life, that you will become active.

230
00:14:52.238 --> 00:14:54.738
We must be the church of Jesus.

231
00:14:55.738 --> 00:15:01.238
And Paul gives his opinion and I find it so nice that the Bible is such an incredibly personal book.

232
00:15:01.738 --> 00:15:10.238
The Bible shows that even in the Bible there are people who share their opinions and say, this is not necessarily the Lord, but this is me.

233
00:15:10.738 --> 00:15:17.238
So when we say that the Bible is 100% God's Word, I personally say amen to that.

234
00:15:17.738 --> 00:15:24.238
But I also see within the Bible that people honestly say of themselves, this is me and not necessarily God.

235
00:15:24.738 --> 00:15:34.238
So the Bible is a very personal book, inspired by God, written by human hands from the experiences and faith-building of people.

236
00:15:34.738 --> 00:15:38.238
And that is the powerful book, the Bible, that we have.

237
00:15:38.738 --> 00:15:42.238
Why is this so important, why am I laying all this out?

238
00:15:42.738 --> 00:15:52.238
Because I also want to tell you that your relationships around you are very contextual.

239
00:15:52.238 --> 00:16:00.738
You have your stuff to deal with in life, you have your things, you have your experiences.

240
